Reject a non-finite shade or alpha value from the config

readDoubleList tests the count of the elements and the success flag of
QString::toDouble. toDouble parses the texts nan, inf and -inf and
reports success, so a value that is not finite passes the only defence
of the function. The value then reaches QColor::setAlphaF and the shade
routine unclamped.

A stored nan paints as an alpha of zero and a stored inf paints as an
alpha of one. The writer stores the same text again, so the value is a
stable state of the file.

Reject an element that is not finite in the same way as an element that
does not parse. The first element then takes zero, which switches the
group off, and the shipped shades and alphas paint.

A reader oracle reads a shade list that starts with nan, and an alpha
list of two infinities, as the off state. The old reader passed both to
the paint code.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 5 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

